 * Diagnostic options shared by every cv4pve .NET CLI tool: added by ConsoleHelper.CreateApp
 * (diag, report, autosnap, pepper, botgram, metrics-exporter) or explicitly (node-protect, cli).
 * Not for vdi (GUI).
 *
 * Verified against cv4pve-api-dotnet v9.2.x: CommandOptionExtension.cs (hidden, recursive options;
 * --log-level overrides --debug), ConsoleHelper.cs (exception details on error), PveClientBase.cs
 * (Debug logs each API call, sensitive parameters masked; Trace logs the full responses).
 * Plain HTML only, so Starlight's content styles apply.
 */
---

<p>
  Two options, not listed in <code>--help</code>, show what the tool is doing. They work before or
  after the command:
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Option</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>--debug</code></td>
      <td>
        On an error, prints the exception type and stack trace after the <code>ERROR:</code> line. Also
        logs each Proxmox VE API call: method, URL, status and duration, and the parameters of calls that
        change data — passwords, tokens and tickets are masked.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>--log-level</code></td>
      <td>
        <code>Trace</code>, <code>Debug</code>, <code>Information</code>, <code>Warning</code> (default),
        <code>Error</code> or <code>Critical</code>; overrides <code>--debug</code>. <code>Trace</code> also
        logs the full API responses — they contain details of your cluster, so review the output before
        sharing it.
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>When you report a problem, attach the output of the failing command run with <code>--debug</code>.</p>
